WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Here's a feminine pocket that little girls

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.000
will just love. The body of
the pocket is gathered.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.080
The lower edge of the pocket is
joined to the sweater as it's knit.

4
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.080
There's a picot hem finishing the top,

5
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.680
and you could knit any hem you
like or even hand knit a few garter rows.

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.720
It's easy to knit, but it does take
some time to rehang the stitches.

7
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.120
So plan a little time for this one.

8
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.520
Once you've established your pocket size
and position,

9
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:41.880
cast-on your A dimension with waste yarn
and ravel cord leaving live stitches.

10
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:49.240
Knit the body of the pocket and remove
the stitches on scrap yarn or a garter bar.

11
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.760
Put the G needles in working position.

12
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.160
And return any other needles
to out of work position.

13
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.280
You'll rehang the scraped off edge of your

14
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.400
pocket on these needles,
gathering them up.

15
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:12.160
Here's a tip to make it easier to finish
the pocket. When you're rehanging,

16
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.760
don't double up a few of those
end needles.

17
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.880
Remove the waste yarn and confirm
that all the stitches are picked up.

18
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.680
With the gathered stitches secure
on the needles,

19
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.920
knit a marker row with the garment yarn
and a marker cord held together.

20
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.760
Use a strong ravel cord
of contrasting color.

21
00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.600
Next, you'll knit across
all of those needles.

22
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.800
Now, there may be three stitches on some

23
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.440
needles, so knit slowly or
knit this row manually.

24
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.120
For  my gauge, I knit five rows

25
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.080
to start my hem,
or about three quarters of an inch.

26
00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:00.600
Knit a turning row, I chose to transfer
every other needle for picots.

27
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.360
Turn your tension down about two full

28
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.040
numbers and knit the second half
of that ham tighter than the garment

29
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:14.560
a tension if you're right-handed, plan to
end this with the carriage on the right.

30
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.080
At this point, turn your tension,

31
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.120
back up to garment
tension before you forget.

32
00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.280
Next, you'll hang the marker row

33
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.480
on the needles,
leave a tail at least three times

34
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.600
the width of the pocket,
breaking the working yarn.

35
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.120
And sew off all those stitches by pulling

36
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.360
that tail of yarn through
each one of the stitches.

37
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.320
We used a double-eye needle,

38
00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.400
but you could use a yarn needle or
a darning needle.

39
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.320
Carefully, remove a few stitches,
pull the tail through,

40
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.280
remove a few more stitches,
pull the tail through and continue

41
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.160
until all the stitches have
been removed from the machine.

42
00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.240
Now, you might be tempted to bind off
these stitches, but by using this method,

43
00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.000
there will be a little more stretch
for the pocket opening so you can get your

44
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.760
hand in. Secure the tail
and remove the marker cord.

45
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.240
And set the pocket aside.
Cast-on and knit your garment

46
00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.840
to the point where you want
the bottom of the pocket to start,

47
00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.640
remove all the stitches from the machine
with a garter bar or scrap them off.

48
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.840
Next, with the knit,
the right or the public side,

49
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.400
whatever you want to call it,
it's the public-facing side of the pocket

50
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:42.560
facing you, hang the lower edge of the
pocket on the corresponding needles.

51
00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:48.480
You're going to hang live stitches
from that ravel cord edge of the pocket.

52
00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:54.200
And as before, you're going to double up
stitches, gathering them in to fit

53
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.960
the number of needles that you need.
You may want to remove the scrap at this

54
00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.120
point and confirm that all the stitches
are securely on the needles.

55
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.160
Make sure that all the stitches
are behind the latches.

56
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.640
Next, rehang the garment on the needle

57
00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.080
bed with the wrong side facing that purl
side needs to be facing you,

58
00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:22.560
putting the garment stitches
in the hooks of the needles.

59
00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.120
Carefully pull those garments stitches

60
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:30.360
through the pocket stitches.
Continue knitting the garment piece.

61
00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.080
When your garment is complete,
finished the pocket by neatly stitching it

62
00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:41.000
in place and voila,
beautiful, feminine, gathered pockets.

